# Interior comment inside an explicit GENERIC-ARGS list — live regression
# pin, on the `Expr::Call` path.
#
# CELL (Core #12): axis = fill-emitted region kind; this file samples the
# `[…]` generic-args region of a call. Its gate is DERIVED — `[` scanned
# forward from the callee end, `]` scanned forward from the last argument
# — because no AST node records the bracket span here (generic PARAMS do,
# which is why they need no scan).
#
# This is also the shape whose sibling the earlier narrow gate was written
# to dodge: the old dispatch clamped its window to the ARGUMENT tuple so a
# generic-args comment could not mis-fire it with the wrong container end.
# The two regions now gate INDEPENDENTLY, each over its own range, so both
# a generic-args comment and an argument comment are preserved — see
# `fmt_delimited_list_interior_comment.gg` for the both-at-once cell.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the pre-fix binary: `# in generic args` dedented out
# of the brackets and became a leading comment of `print(x[0])` —
#     auto x = foo[int, String](42)
#     # in generic args
#     print(x[0])

Vector[int] foo[T, U](int x):
    return [x]

void main():
    auto x = foo[
        int,
        # in generic args
        String,
    ](42)
    print(x[0])
